hello there you're watching a game spot  news update with me sub Ford the  PlayStation 4's project Morpheus virtual  reality device won't cost you a thousand  dollars but also won't be arriving in  2014 PlayStation president of worldwide  studios Shuhei Yoshida told GameSpot  today at GDC that Sony engineers are  continuing to iterate on a device and  they won't have a feature complete  version ready anytime soon we asked  Yoshida directly if a 2014 launch date  for project Morpheus had been ruled out  and his response was quote yes that we  can say comfortably because we are still  making changes to the hardware the  PlayStation executive also addressed the  matter of pricing for project Morpheus  saying you won't have to spend a  thousand dollars to get your hands on  the device as is the case with Sony's  hmz head-mounted display line Yoshida  said Sony often prices its gaming  hardware lower than other non-gaming  Sony devices and explained that he  doesn't expect this to change with  project Morpheus as such Yoshida  explained that a thousand dollar price  point doesn't necessarily indicate the  pricing that we're going to have for  project Morpheus as for the competition  oculus rift creator Palmer Luckey is  said earlier this month that he wants  his device to be affordable so as not to  be a rich person's toy but what's your  choice between Morpheus and oculus and  do you think that VR is the future of  gaming do let me know in the comments  below and for a complete comparison  between the two devices head over to our  hub at gamespot.com /g DC
 

